        "answer": {
          "short": "$2:3$; $\\frac{2}{3}$ is the largest cordial-to-water fraction.",
          "worked": "Compare cordial as a fraction of water:\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5}&=\\frac{6}{30}\\\\\\frac{2}{5}&=\\frac{12}{30}\\\\\\frac{2}{3}&=\\frac{20}{30}\\\\\\frac{3}{10}&=\\frac{9}{30}\\end{aligned}$$\nThe largest fraction is $\\frac{2}{3}$, so $2:3$ gives the most cordial for the same amount of water and makes the strongest drink.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
